 "notes": "GA: AP called all 14 races (FOX 5 Atlanta). GA-1: Kingston won by about 2.9 points; Democrat Amanda Hollowell had not conceded and said she would challenge the result. GA-13: Everton Blair Jr. (sitting, won special election) did not win the full term; Jasmine Clark was called the winner. GA-14 Clay Fuller is sitting (won April special). NC: results unofficial; state canvass Nov 24, recount requests due noon Nov 17. NC-5 marked uncalled: Democrat Chuck Hubbard leads Rep. Virginia Foxx (R) by 331 votes after county canvass (WRAL, Nov 13); Foxx has not conceded; recount-eligible. NC-7 marked uncalled: Rep. David Rouzer (R) leads Kimberly Hardy (D) by 2,311 votes, not called by AP per WRAL, recount-eligible. NC-10 marked uncalled: Rep. Pat Harrigan (R) leads Ashley Bell (D) by 2,509 votes, not called per WRAL, recount-eligible. NC-3: Raymond Smith (D) led Murphy by about 300 votes after provisional ballots; WRAL reports Murphy conceded; marked called on that basis though margin is within recount range. NC-8 Harris AP call taken from Axios search snippet (page itself returned 403). NC-2/4/12 incumbent reelections from Carolina Journal Nov 4 roundup. Backgrounds for Kingston, Gaines, Ager, Smith, Barringer, Womack come from search-result summaries of news pages rather than full page reads."
